4. Local modifications
----------------------

4.1 Files not bundled

Only the files listed in tools/highway-files.txt (package sources) are
copied from upstream. Left out:

  hwy/tests/, *_test.cc, hwy/examples/, g3doc/, docs/, and the CMake, Bazel,
  Meson and Debian build files
      Not needed to compile against the headers.
  hwy/contrib/sort/
      Needs about 22 separately compiled per-type sources (vqsort_*.cc).
  hwy/contrib/thread_pool/, hwy/contrib/matvec/
      Create their own threads (CRAN limits checks to two cores) and print
      diagnostics to stdout/stderr; matvec depends on thread_pool.
  hwy/contrib/random/
      A random number generator; Writing R Extensions asks packages not to
      use third-party RNGs in compiled code. Also under CC0, not the dual
      licence.
  hwy/nanobenchmark.*, hwy/profiler.*, hwy/perf_counters.*, hwy/stats.*,
  hwy/timer*, hwy/robust_statistics.h, hwy/auto_tune.h, hwy/print*
      Benchmarking and debugging helpers that print to stdout/stderr or need
      extra compiled sources; not used by the bundled headers.
  hwy/ops/ppc_vsx-inl.h, hwy/ops/rvv-inl.h, hwy/ops/loongarch_lsx-inl.h,
  hwy/ops/loongarch_lasx-inl.h, hwy/ops/wasm_128-inl.h, hwy/ops/wasm_256-inl.h
      SIMD back ends for POWER/s390x, RISC-V, LoongArch and WebAssembly,
      left out to keep the installed package under CRAN's 5 MB size
      threshold. On those architectures inst/include/highway/config.h
      restricts Highway to its portable EMU128 target, so code still
      compiles and runs correctly there, without native vector
      instructions.

4.2 Patches

The patches listed in section 2 are kept as separate files in tools/patches/
of the package sources and are applied by tools/update_highway.sh. Each
changed location in the bundled files is marked with a comment beginning
"R package 'highway' (local patch NNNN)". In summary:

  0001  The default abort handler throws highway::abort_error instead of
        printing to stderr and calling abort() or exit(); the default
        warning handler is silent.
  0002  Highway's runtime symbols get hidden visibility, so copies compiled
        into different packages stay separate.
  0003  hwy/detect_targets.h includes highway/config.h and honours
        HIGHWAY_R_BROKEN_TARGETS.
  0004  HWY_WARN/HWY_ABORT no longer use the GNU ',##__VA_ARGS__' extension.
  0005  __uint128_t replaces 'unsigned __int128' (ISO C++ pedantic warning).
  0006  sizeof(v.raw) replaces a template use that triggered
        -Wignored-attributes.
  0007  Highway's diagnostic-suppression pragmas are compiled out for GCC
        and Clang (CRAN policy).
  0008  On MinGW (Rtools), format strings are checked with the GNU printf
        archetype, avoiding false -Wformat warnings for %zu.
  0009  On Arm NEON with GCC, Undefined() returns a zero vector instead of an
        uninitialised one (GCC -Wmaybe-uninitialized).


